body: "## Static finding in shipped code and current main\n\nPublished `pm-linear@2026.10.3` (npm gitHead `cb914b21798d7b5e1dc5830af09737469d2448d8`) and main `55ed55fcd6086865aa39e4da03a9899b2f03de21` both use this [local reader](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/55ed55fcd6086865aa39e4da03a9899b2f03de21/index.ts#L1124):\n\n```ts\n[\"--path\", pmRoot, \"--json\", \"list\", \"--full\", \"--include-body\", \"--limit\", \"10000\"]\n// after a zero exit:\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(result.stdout);\nconst items = Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : parsed.items ?? parsed.results ?? [];\nreturn items as PmItem[];\n```\n\nThe 16 MiB buffer only bounds transport. The reader does not request all statuses or strict/unbounded output and never validates pagination, source completeness, field omissions, or universal output-budget receipts.\n\n## Failure mechanism and impact\n\nThe exact decoder accepts\n`{items:[{id:\"fixture-1\"}], count:1, total:10001, truncated:true, has_more:true, next_cursor:\"more\"}`\nas a whole corpus. A missing `items` field becomes an empty success.\n\nThe existing Linear-provenance index then misses local matches, risking duplicate creation on sync; export can silently omit tasks. This differs from remote GraphQL pagination: even a fully fetched remote result is reconciled against an uncertified local subset.\n\nThis is **source/artifact evidence**, not a live Linear reproduction. The review environment denied child-process fixtures with `spawnSync … EPERM`; those tests were stopped. No Linear API request, paid call, or private transmission was performed.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nUse public SDK `listAllComplete`, or certify canonical strict/all-status/full/unbounded responses. Refuse partial/malformed/missing/compacted/omitted answers before mutations. Cover >10,000 local items, matching closed/canceled work, degraded output receipts and re-import idempotency. An in-process public SDK reader also removes the extra CLI launch and full JSON serialization overhead; retain correct complete selection when introducing projections or streaming.\n\nDuplicate check: all-status GitHub issue/PR pages and main PM tracker checked October 5; no corresponding open fix. [pm-linear-92kd](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/55ed55fcd6086865aa39e4da03a9899b2f03de21/.agents/pm/issues/pm-linear-92kd.toon) fixed remote GraphQL pagination; [pm-linear-4so4](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/55ed55fcd6086865aa39e4da03a9899b2f03de21/.agents/pm/issues/pm-linear-4so4.toon) fixed changelog reads. Neither certifies this local integration reader.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-05T11:40:07Z)\n>\n> Rechecked the newly published `pm-linear@2026.10.5` (npm gitHead `79176f2d4b112d5aad15491e358e47349ffe4423`; registry tarball SHA-512/SHA-1 verified). The local-reader finding remains applicable.\n> \n> The [readPmItems helper](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/79176f2d4b112d5aad15491e358e47349ffe4423/index.ts#L1124-L1143) is byte-for-byte unchanged from the 2026.10.3 artifact after matching the helper boundary. It still uses the bounded `--limit 10000` selection and returns parsed `items`/`results` without validating complete-read evidence.\n> \n> Call-site scope is confirmed for both the [sync index](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/79176f2d4b112d5aad15491e358e47349ffe4423/index.ts#L1757-L1761) and [exporter](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/blob/79176f2d4b112d5aad15491e358e47349ffe4423/index.ts#L2955-L2965). The existing remote GraphQL pagination and changelog-read fixes remain distinct.\n> \n> This is source and shipped-artifact evidence only. No live Linear calls, provider writes, large-corpus runtime or re-import/idempotency test was performed; the issue's current acceptance remains open."
